markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 5: Loop Basics</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 7-8</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach two curriculum lessons. For loops and while loops are really one skill, loop syntax, taught across two lessons, so this section walks through both in parallel: same structure for each, concept, interactive walkthrough, practice, and the misconception to watch for.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 7:</b> Simulation (Part 1)</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_7_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 7</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 8:</b> Simulation (Part 2)</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_8_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 8</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Walk through for loops and the range function, then step through an actual execution one iteration at a time</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Trace a for-loop example yourself in the Python Lab before watching students do the same</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of the off-by-one mistake, the single most common loop error, before it shows up live</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; See how while loops differ from for loops, and why their condition works differently</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of infinite loops, usually caused by forgetting to update the condition, and know when to reach for while instead of for</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> for and while loops aren't two unrelated topics, they're one idea, repetition, with two different ways of deciding when to stop. Keeping that framing in mind will help you answer "which one do I use here?" questions quickly.</div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
